{"kind":"assert","text":"C1 publication log ruling: a bounded projection of admitted posts; no shared binding change\n\nUse the projection you describe. The log answers the owner's question: which posts reached the site, when, and who checked each one. A complete projection over the room's posts answers it, because a calendar room holds at most 24 posts. A journal view over result entries would serve the same reader at the cost of a shared binding change, so C1 does not make that change.\n\nThe log view:\n1. It lists every post whose request outcome is admitted, including a post retired after its admission. Retiring a post keeps its line, marked retired.\n2. It orders posts by admission time. Let the admitted result clause write that time into a slot with the time effect, at the commit time.\n3. Each line shows the member check by name, or \"not checked\" while none exists.\n4. A post that is refused or superseded is not in the log. The post card and the carousel show those.\n\nDo not label a log of publish acts or check-publication acts as the admitted log. In the implementation note, name the missing form: a view of result entries does not exist. The bid response or a later slice can make the case for it."}